Extract lab results from a medical lab report into a JSON array.

Output format:
[
  { "label": "718-7", "value": 15.5, "unit": "g%" },
  { "label": "18311-0", "value": "normocytic, normochromic", "unit": null }
]

LABELS
- Use the LOINC code as the label (e.g. "718-7" for hemoglobin, "6690-2"
  for WBC, "1742-6" for ALT).
- If you do not know the LOINC code for a test, use the full English name
  in snake_case with specimen suffix (_blood, _urine, _smear) as fallback.

VALUES
- Numeric results must be JSON numbers, not strings.
- Text results (qualitative findings) must be lowercase strings.
- Extract only the patient result. Ignore reference ranges and flag columns.

MORPHOLOGY / SMEAR
- Smear and morphology findings are valid results; include them with a _smear suffix.
- Store the finding as a lowercase string. Never invent a numeric value for a morphology finding.

UNITS
- Set unit to null when no unit is present.

OUTPUT
- Return only the raw JSON array. No explanation, no markdown, no code fences.